**Strongest hit (FUTURE-H1):** the pattern-over-peg architecture. The thesis rides three walk-aways across 36 years, not the August 2026 news peg — remove the newest event and the piece still stands, which is exactly what a twelve-months-later reader needs. The draft also pre-registers its own falsifier in the Rabbit Hole ("If future reporting showed… the step-down was forced and spun, the 3 case would deserve a rehearing"), and my research confirmed it quietly dodged a trap: it never repeats Hassabis's Isomorphic trials-timeline promise, which had already slipped once ([Reuters via Investing.com](https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/googlebacked-ai-drug-discovery-startup-isomorphic-labs-delays-clinical-trial-timeline-4456134)).

**Blocker (FUTURE-R1):** the Liechtenstein origin scene narrates "a veteran Danish master" and "around 1987" as fact, while the evidence packet's Althöfer 2024 entry says the opponent was a ~25-year-old German FM at a tournament with no Danish players. As Hassabis's profile keeps rising, this published correction is the most likely "well, actually" to surface within the year. Cheap, outcome-proof repair: attribute the particulars to his own telling and drop "veteran Danish."

**Highest-priority concern (FUTURE-C6):** the "tanks on the lawn" pull quote and the Silver quote both ride a single LessWrong reviewer's transcription of the Mallaby book — verify against the printed book before publish. Close behind: a small family of unanchored live-state claims ("still leads Isomorphic Labs," "Wikipedia manages one sentence," the second-workday present tense, "He is fifty.") that will go stale inside the window; the review includes clause-level repairs and a dated twelve-month refresh list. Post-announcement coverage through August 29 ([Time](https://time.com/article/2026/08/06/google-deepmind-ai-demis-hassabis/), [Axios](https://www.axios.com/2026/08/06/googles-ai-leadership-shuffle), [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/06/demis-hassabis-google-reshuffle-deepmind-role.html), [Fortune](https://fortune.com/2026/08/05/demis-hassabis-steps-down-google-deepmind-ai-shakeup/)) shows nothing that dates the draft yet.
